// Title: Dllhost.EXE Initiated Network Connection To Non-Local IP Address
// Sigma ID: cfed2f44-16df-4bf3-833a-79405198b277
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: bartblaze
// Date: 2020-07-13 | Modified: 2024-07-16
// ATT&CK: stealth, T1218, execution, T1559.001
// Tags: detection.threat-hunting
// Description: Detects Dllhost.EXE initiating a network connection to a non-local IP address. Aside from
//   Microsoft own IP range that needs to be excluded. Network communication from Dllhost will depend
//   entirely on the hosted DLL. An initial baseline is recommended before deployment.
// False positives:
//   - Communication to other corporate systems that use IP addresses from public address spaces
// References:
//   - https://redcanary.com/blog/child-processes/
//   - https://nasbench.medium.com/what-is-the-dllhost-exe-process-actually-running-ef9fe4c19c08
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules-threat-hunting/windows/network_connection/net_connection_win_dllhost_non_local_ip.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, microsoft_xdr schema)

DeviceNetworkEvents
| where InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\dllhost.exe" and (not(((ipv4_is_in_range(RemoteIP, "::1/128") or ipv4_is_in_range(RemoteIP, "10.0.0.0/8") or ipv4_is_in_range(RemoteIP, "127.0.0.0/8") or ipv4_is_in_range(RemoteIP, "172.16.0.0/12") or ipv4_is_in_range(RemoteIP, "192.168.0.0/16") or ipv4_is_in_range(RemoteIP, "169.254.0.0/16") or ipv4_is_in_range(RemoteIP, "fc00::/7") or ipv4_is_in_range(RemoteIP, "fe80::/10")) or (ipv4_is_in_range(RemoteIP, "20.184.0.0/13") or ipv4_is_in_range(RemoteIP, "20.192.0.0/10") or ipv4_is_in_range(RemoteIP, "23.72.0.0/13") or ipv4_is_in_range(RemoteIP, "51.10.0.0/15") or ipv4_is_in_range(RemoteIP, "51.103.0.0/16") or ipv4_is_in_range(RemoteIP, "51.104.0.0/15") or ipv4_is_in_range(RemoteIP, "52.224.0.0/11") or ipv4_is_in_range(RemoteIP, "150.171.0.0/19") or ipv4_is_in_range(RemoteIP, "204.79.197.0/24")))))
